  friday: {
    title:"Show What You Know: Week 20",
    reading:"This week you studied the War of 1812, the Black defenders of New Orleans, and the diversity and reproduction of plants. Show what you remember, then make your case about the war's meaning.",
    groups:[
      {type:"choice", instructions:"Choose the best answer for each question.", items:[
        {id:"f-c1", prompt:"Francis Scott Key wrote the national anthem after watching...", options:["the British bombardment of Fort McHenry","the Battle of New Orleans","the burning of Washington"], answer:"the British bombardment of Fort McHenry"},
        {id:"f-c2", prompt:"The Black battalions at New Orleans were made up of...", options:["free Black militiamen from Louisiana","British defectors","French mercenaries"], answer:"free Black militiamen from Louisiana"},
        {id:"f-c3", prompt:"Angiosperms are best defined as...", options:["flowering plants with seeds enclosed in fruit","mosses without true roots","seedless ferns"], answer:"flowering plants with seeds enclosed in fruit"}
      ]},
      {type:"truefalse", instructions:"Decide whether each statement is true or false.", items:[
        {id:"f-t1", text:"The Battle of New Orleans was fought after the Treaty of Ghent had been signed.", answer:"true", note:"News of the treaty had not yet crossed the Atlantic."},
        {id:"f-t2", text:"Mosses can grow tall because they have true water-carrying veins.", answer:"false", note:"Mosses lack true veins, which keeps them small and tied to damp places."}
      ]},
      {type:"matching", instructions:"Match each term to its meaning.", options:[{key:"a", text:"Strong pride in one's nation"},{key:"b", text:"Song representing a nation"},{key:"c", text:"Plant producing seeds without flowers"},{key:"d", text:"Transfer of pollen between flowers"}], items:[
        {id:"f-m1", term:"nationalism", answer:"a"},
        {id:"f-m2", term:"anthem", answer:"b"}
      ]},
      {type:"shortanswer", instructions:"Write 4-6 sentences, then compare your answer with the model.", items:[
        {id:"f-s1", prompt:"Argue: What is the true meaning of the War of 1812: a pointless war that proved nothing, or the victory that made America a real nation? Defend your answer.", answer:"The War of 1812 was the victory that made America feel like a real nation, even though it changed little on paper. The Treaty of Ghent restored prewar borders, so critics call the war pointless. But the failed invasions, the defense of Baltimore, and Jackson's triumph at New Orleans gave Americans a shared story of standing up to Britain. The war killed the Federalist Party and launched an era of nationalism. A nation is partly a story its people believe, and the War of 1812 gave Americans a story of independence confirmed."}
      ]}
    ]
  },
