        {id:"f-s1", prompt:"Argue: Was Reconstruction's promise of land betrayed, or was it never a real promise at all? Use evidence from Special Field Orders No. 15 and its reversal.", answer:"The promise of land was betrayed, because it was a real policy that freed people acted on before it was taken away. Special Field Orders No. 15 reserved coastal land for freed families, and roughly 40,000 people settled plots of up to forty acres and began farming. Garrison Frazier told Sherman directly that land was how freed people could best care for themselves, which shows the promise matched their deepest need. Then President Johnson ordered the land returned to former Confederate owners, forcing families off farms they had started. A promise that is made, relied upon, and then revoked is not an illusion; it is a betrayal."}
