            {id:"h2-t2", text:"Black workers in Birmingham labored in coal mines, iron mines, and steel furnaces.", answer:"true", note:"Black labor built the South's new steel industry from the ground up."},
            {id:"h2-t3", text:"Most industrial workers in the Gilded Age could support a family comfortably on their wages.", answer:"false", note:"Wages were low, hours were long, and many families sent children to work."}
