            {id:"h1-c2", prompt:"How did the Great Migration help build Black prosperity in the 1920s?", options:["It moved families to factory cities with better wages and dense Black neighborhoods like Harlem", "It returned families to Southern farms", "It closed Black-owned businesses"], answer:"It moved families to factory cities with better wages and dense Black neighborhoods like Harlem"},
            {id:"h1-c3", prompt:"Why does the reading call the boom 'narrower and shakier' than headlines suggested?", options:["Farmers were already in a depression and the market rested on borrowed money", "No one bought automobiles", "Radios had not been invented"], answer:"Farmers were already in a depression and the market rested on borrowed money"}
