            {id:"h2-t2", text:"The Johnson-Reed Act of 1924 opened American borders to all immigrants.", answer:"false", note:"It set strict quotas designed to preserve a white, Northern European America."},
            {id:"h2-t3", text:"Langston Hughes argued that Black artists should seek white approval.", answer:"false", note:"Hughes wrote that Black artists should express themselves 'without fear or shame.'"}
