        {id:"f-s1", prompt:"Argue: the 80s verdict. Was the Reagan era a success for America? Take a clear position and support it with at least two pieces of evidence from this week's lessons.", answer:"The Reagan era was a mixed verdict rather than a clear success. Reagan's combination of military strength and diplomacy helped end the Cold War peacefully, and his policies pulled the economy out of 1970s stagflation. Yet the war on drugs he escalated imposed mandatory minimums and a 100-to-1 crack-to-powder disparity that devastated Black communities through mass incarceration. The national debt tripled at the same time, leaving future taxpayers the bill. The decade delivered confidence and victory abroad, but its domestic toll means the verdict must stay complicated."}
